      "challenges": [
        "2,441 alerts; 2,393 verified (98.0%), 514 validated suspects, 514 investigated (100.0%), and 255 transferred. Six provinces have numeric alert rows (Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Ituri, Nord-Kivu, Sud-Ubangi and Tshopo); Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero.",
        "Nord-Kivu prints 383 hospitalised patients, 271 of them in normed structures, and 63.0% occupancy without a bed count. 63.0% matches neither basis against the 354 beds SR135 last printed (271/354 is 76.6%; 383/354 is 108.2%) and repeats the 63.0% printed in SR135, SR136 and SR138, so the rate is withheld as a conflict. 112 patients (29.2%) are outside normed structures.",
        "Contact follow-up 25,277/31,092 (81.3%). Six reporting province rows sum to the national contact line; Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero. The national rate moved from 80.6% the day before, and no province followed all of its contacts.",
        "PoE/PoC completeness is 97/99 (98.0%). Of seven PoE/PoC alerts, four at the Epulu Zunguluka PoC (Mambasa) were validated; three were transferred to the Mambasa CTE and the fourth chose care at Mangina (75.0%). A body intercepted at the Dele PoC (Rwampara) went to the morgue for a swab, and the Maboya PoC (Kalunguta) alert was validated and referred to CH Tinge.",
        "Ituri ring opening is 18/29 (62.1%); 27 bodies were not swabbed for lack of supplies and teams at Mandima or after family refusals. Nord-Kivu household decontamination is 10/24 (41.7%)."
      ],
